You can modify the code to display a new quote automatically every 10 seconds by using the setInterval() method. Here's the modified code:
```
const quotes = [
  {
    "quote": "Be the change you wish to see in the world.",
    "author": "Mahatma Gandhi"
  },
  {
    "quote": "Success is not final, failure is not fatal: It is the courage to continue that counts.",
    "author": "Winston Churchill"
  },
  {
    "quote": "Believe you can and you're halfway there.",
    "author": "Theodore Roosevelt"
  },
  {
    "quote": "The only way to do great work is to love what you do.",
    "author": "Steve Jobs"
  },
  {
    "quote": "Don't watch the clock; do what it does. Keep going.",
    "author": "Sam Levenson"
  }
];
function displayQuote() {
  const randomQuote = quotes[Math.floor(Math.random() * quotes.length)];
  const quoteElement = document.getElementById("quote");
  const authorElement = document.getElementById("author");
  quoteElement.innerText = randomQuote.quote;
  authorElement.innerText = "- " + randomQuote.author;
}
// Display a new quote every 10 seconds
setInterval(displayQuote, 10000);
```
In this code, the setInterval() method is used to call the displayQuote() function every 10 seconds (10000 milliseconds). This will automatically update the quote and author displayed on the webpage without the need for user interaction.

